-- 184_postmatch_host_reentry.surql -- the Fighting Collection post-match flow is HOST-DRIVEN and the
-- host ends it by RE-ENTERING the mode (fresh arena carve), measured live 2026-09-05.
-- Forward slashes only in ref/note strings.
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:postmatch_probe_20260905 SET kind='capture', strength='reproduction',
  ref='d3dcap/ttd/probe_win.py (read-only ReadProcessMemory at ~120 Hz, prints on change) against the live MarvelVsCapcomFightingCollection.exe pid 31512 through one Versus match, select -> battle -> 1P WIN -> host victory menu -> Rematch -> select; log d3dcap/ttd/probe_win.log. Decompiles: FUN_140611A20 (+disassembly), FUN_14060E170, FUN_140614B70, FUN_140614CC0, FUN_140614FA0, FUN_140615760, FUN_140615930, FUN_140615A40, FUN_140631E10, FUN_140631EB0, FUN_140632370, FUN_1406320B0, FUN_140037B50, FUN_14062BC80, FUN_14062E090, FUN_14061D900; exe_image.bin reads of the tables 0x140A6BFC8, 0x140A6BFD8, 0x140A6C040, 0x140A73178, 0x140A73788. Runner: supergun sg_runner PHASE log (sg_play/runner.log).',
  note='SUPERGUN parked on the 1P WIN screen forever (RUNNING, not a fault). Live trace: select G=[2,1,1,3] -> battle [2,1,2,2..3] -> 1P WIN [2,1,2,4,1] with G+8 = 540 counting down -> at G+8 == 210: config+0x7D0 1->0, +0x7E0 0->1, G+0xE = 1 -> (host victory menu, Rematch) -> blk pointer 0x17ac1000 -> 0x17dc1000, G all zero (G+0x2A 0, G+0x44 1), config+0x840 = 2, then 7D0 = 1, 7E0 = 0, G -> [2,1,0] -> [2,1,1,0] -> [2,1,1,1] -> [2,1,1,3] = select, clock restarted at 0.';

UPSERT finding:phase_dispatch_tables SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-05',
  title='The top-level phase dispatch: FUN_140611A20 switches on G+1 (table 0x140A6BFC8); under G+1 == 1 the G+2 table 0x140A6BFD8 is [1] select, [2] battle, [3] post-match; the battle sub-machine is FUN_14060E170 on G+3/G+4',
  statement='FUN_140611A20: FUN_14062E090 (coin/credit UI, returns early when G+0x2A != 0 or G+0x4C == 2); G+0x80++; FUN_140619840 (copies the seat words blk+0x3C66.. into the six fighter input mirrors); jmp 0x140A6BFC8[G+1]. G+1 == 0 body 0x140611B70 = mode init; G+1 == 1 body 0x140611D60 = call 0x140A6BFD8[G+2]; G+1 == 2 body 0x140611D90 = G+2 = 1, G+3..7 = 0, G+0x9A = 1, FUN_140608BF0 (back to select). G+2 table: [0] 0x140611D90, [1] FUN_140628D60 (SELECT: dispatches PTR_FUN_140A6FB00[G+3], seed 175), [2] FUN_14060E170 (BATTLE), [3] FUN_140631E10 (POST-MATCH: PTR_FUN_140A73178[G+3]), [4] FUN_140632510 (0x140A73788[G+4]), [5] FUN_140632160, [6] 0x140611A80 (reset to title). FUN_14060E170 by G+3: 0 round init, 1 pre-round, 2 VS intro (FUN_140628570), 3 = sub-switch on G+4 (0 load, 1 round init, 2 the ROUND, 4 match cleanup: G+2++ -> 3, G+3 = 0, G+8 = 0x438; 5 countdown -> G+1++), 4 = FUN_140614B70 = the WIN SCREEN (0x140A6C040[G+4]: [0] FUN_140614C30 enter, [1] FUN_140614CC0 the screen, [2] FUN_140614FA0 -> G+2 = 3 post-match, [3] FUN_140615760 REMATCH with the saved teams (G+3 = 4), [4] FUN_140615930 countdown, [5] FUN_140615A40 G+1 = 1, G+2 = 0 -> select), default = match-end tally. FUN_14060BA00 queues a draw callback into 0x142EC6780[16] drained by FUN_14060B960 inside the build FUN_140608A00 (not the flush).',
  consequence='Ghidra jumptable labels on these switches are unreliable (truncated jumptables); the tables were read from exe_image.bin and the bodies mapped by disassembly. The measured live G sequence matches this map exactly.';

UPSERT finding:win_screen_is_host_driven SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-05',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='The 1P WIN screen FUN_140614CC0 never advances when config+0x7C0 != 0 (Versus AND Arcade): it counts G+8 540->0, reports the winner into config+0x7E0 at G+8 == 210, and waits for the HOST',
  statement='FUN_140614CC0 (G+3 == 4, G+4 == 1) branches on config+0x7C0. config+0x7C0 == 0 (the original DC flow): advances G+4 on a button (seat word & 0x360 with G+0xE != 0) or when G+8 hits 0, -> FUN_140614FA0 -> G+2 = 3 post-match screens. config+0x7C0 != 0: G+0x19 = 1; if G+8 > 0 G+8--; at G+8 == 0x168 G+0xE = 1; at G+8 == 0xD2 && config+0x7D0 != 0: config+0x7E0 = *(DAT_142EDF628+0x5E) + 1 (winner side + 1), config+0x7D0 = 0; then FUN_14061CA70 / FUN_140610730 -- no write to G+4 anywhere. FUN_140037B50 (mode ladder) sets config+0x7C0 = 1 for Versus (config+0x80C != 0, from session+0xD0338) and Arcade (config+0x828 == 1) alike, so this is the Fighting Collection design, not an anchor quirk. Ghidra xrefs to the G pointer 0x142EDF580: every reference is in the game module; no host code loads it. Measured live: G+8 reached 210 with 7D0 = 1 -> 7D0 = 0, 7E0 = 1, then nothing changed in G until the host acted.',
  consequence='A shell that runs only the game tick sits on the win screen forever (SUPERGUN: G=[2,1,2,4,1], G+8 = 0, RUNNING). The exit is the host action, not a game state.';

UPSERT finding:host_postmatch_reentry SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-05',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='After its victory menu the host ends the match by RE-ENTERING the mode: a fresh arena carve (new blk), G from zero to select, with config+0x840 = 2, +0x7D0 = 1, +0x7E0 = 0',
  statement='Measured live (probe_win.log): 6 s after the result report (the user on the collection victory menu choosing Rematch) the blk pointer changed 0x17ac1000 -> 0x17dc1000 (a new FUN_140607B50 carve), G read all zero (G+0x2A = 0, G+0x44 = 1 = fresh), config+0x840 went 1 -> 2, then config+0x7D0 = 1 and +0x7E0 = 0, and G went [2,1,0,0] -> [2,1,1,0] -> [2,1,1,1] (G+8 = 99) -> [2,1,1,3] = character select with the clock restarted at 0. config+0x840 == 2 makes the select entry FUN_14062BC80 restore the win tallies: blk+0x447B = config[0x5B8], blk+0x4BB3 = config[0x5BC] (the counts the victory menu shows). The host never wrote G+4: G+4 = 1 on the win screen was still 1 in the last pre-re-entry sample.',
  consequence='SUPERGUN re-entry = the same thing the runner does at start-up: put the select anchor back (blk, blk2, ctx, dcram, and the game global page 0x142EDF300..+0x400 from exe_image.bin), write config+0x840 = 2, +0x7D0 = 1, +0x7E0 = 0, and -- because the anchor is post-entry (G+3 = 3) -- apply the two tally bytes FUN_14062BC80 would have. Implemented as win_screen_done() / reenter_select() in sg_runner main.rs, triggered as soon as G+2 = 2, G+3 = 4, G+4 = 1 with config+0x7C0 != 0 (the user chose to skip the game own 9 s win screen; the host menu itself is not reproduced).',
  caveat='Restoring the anchor is the runner stand-in for the game own mode entry (Gate 3, arc -> DC-RAM from scratch, is not built). The game .data outside the 0x400 global page is left as the match left it; whether that matters is gated by the select working after re-entry (PHASE log), not assumed.';

RELATE finding:phase_dispatch_tables->cites->source:postmatch_probe_20260905 SET id='e184_tables_src';
RELATE finding:win_screen_is_host_driven->cites->source:postmatch_probe_20260905 SET id='e184_win_src';
RELATE finding:host_postmatch_reentry->cites->source:postmatch_probe_20260905 SET id='e184_reentry_src';
RELATE finding:host_postmatch_reentry->cites->finding:win_screen_is_host_driven SET id='e184_reentry_win';
RELATE finding:win_screen_is_host_driven->cites->finding:mode_lives_in_host_device_session SET id='e184_win_mode';
RELATE finding:phase_dispatch_tables->cites->finding:select_dispatch_tables SET id='e184_tables_select';

UPDATE finding:phase_dispatch_tables SET status='confirmed';
UPDATE finding:win_screen_is_host_driven SET status='confirmed';
UPDATE finding:host_postmatch_reentry SET status='confirmed';
